<title>UK: Flextech chief Luard says no plans to quit.</title>
<headline>Flextech chief Luard says no plans to quit.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Flextech Plc denied on Monday weekend press reports that its chief executive Roger Luard was to leave the company.</p>
<p>Denying a Sunday Express report Luard said: &quot;I remain committed to Flextech and have no plans to leave. I fully intend to be involved in Flextech's continued growth and development&quot;.</p>
<p>Flextech's share price had fallen 19 pence to 634 before Luard's assurance came. It was last traded at 636p at 1450 GMT.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
